            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="da">Ved Graven, hvor i bliver hensat Fordum den stormægtigste Monarch, nu hos Gud høyst-salige Konge og Herre, Kong Christian den Siette</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_d6814257">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_21">Peder Sparkiær</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_1c16c22b">King Christian VI</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_22_0">
               <date isodate="1746" xml:id="date_63c4c18c">1746</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_22_0">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_22_0">
               <p xml:id="idm120">For the funeral of <persName xml:id="idm121" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Christian VI</persName> who died in autumn 1746, Scheibe composed the present rather short cantata which was performed on 5 October in Roskilde Cathedral, thirty kilometres west of Copenhagen. The text was by <persName xml:id="idm122" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peder Sparkiær</persName> who had often provided texts for official events at the court. The music has not survived. The text is identical to nos. 8–12 of the cantata performed at the University of Copenhagen on the previous day (cf. SchW B2:443. It seems most likely that the music was also identical.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_62350d8d">
